[TestRateVMMeasuredInterval/rate_prometheus_with_the_measured_interval - 1]
- description: rate_prometheus with the measured interval
  content: |
    - record: foo:rate
      expr: rate_prometheus(foo[5m])
  output: |
    2 |   expr: rate_prometheus(foo[5m])
                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
                `rate_prometheus()` needs a window of at least 20m with samples of `foo` every 10m on `prom`
                VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com (its slowest series in the last 15m,
                measured with `scrape_interval()`; `scrapeInterval` in pint config is 1m):
                `rate_prometheus()` follows Prometheus semantics and only uses samples inside the window, so
                it needs 2 scrape intervals. A `[5m]` window can have a single sample, so it can return no
                results or wrong ones.
  problem:
    reporter: promql/rate
    summary: duration too small
    details: 'vmalert evaluates rules with instant queries and sends `-datasource.queryStep` as the step, 5m by default, or `step` from the group `params`. VictoriaMetrics only uses the last sample before the window if it''s at most one step before the window. With a scrape interval longer than the step a window shorter than two scrape intervals minus the step can have a single sample: `rate()` and `irate()` return nothing and `increase()` returns 0. `deriv()` only uses samples inside the window and always needs two scrape intervals.'
    diagnostics:
        - message: '`rate_prometheus()` needs a window of at least 20m with samples of `foo` every 10m on `prom` VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com (its slowest series in the last 15m, measured with `scrape_interval()`; `scrapeInterval` in pint config is 1m): `rate_prometheus()` follows Prometheus semantics and only uses samples inside the window, so it needs 2 scrape intervals. A `[5m]` window can have a single sample, so it can return no results or wrong ones.'
          firstcolumn: 1
          lastcolumn: 24
          kind: 0
