[TestRateVMMeasuredInterval/window_derived_from_the_step_with_the_measured_interval - 1]
- description: window derived from the step with the measured interval
  content: |
    - record: foo:rate
      expr: rate(foo)
  output: |
    2 |   expr: rate(foo)
                ^^^^^^^^^
                `rate()` has no lookbehind window, so VictoriaMetrics uses a 5m window, the query step,
                default vmalert -datasource.queryStep (5m). `rate()` needs a window of at least 15m with
                samples of `foo` every 10m on `prom` VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com
                (its slowest series in the last 15m, measured with `scrape_interval()`; `scrapeInterval` in
                pint config is 1m), so it can return no results or wrong ones.
  problem:
    reporter: promql/rate
    summary: duration too small
    details: |-
        Using [rate](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/metricsql/#rate), [irate](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/metricsql/#irate) and [increase](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/metricsql/#increase) functions comes with a few requirements:

        - The metric you calculate (i)rate or increase from must be a counter or a native histogram.
        - The time window of the (i)rate or increase function must have at least 1 sample.

        VictoriaMetrics also uses the last sample before the time window when calculating `rate()`, `irate()`, `increase()` and `deriv()`,
        so the minimal time window you can use is one scrape interval.
        `rate_prometheus()` and `increase_prometheus()` follow Prometheus semantics and need at least two scrape intervals.

        Without a lookbehind window, like `rate(foo)`, or with a window relative to the step, like `rate(foo[2i])`, the window depends on the query step. vmalert evaluates rules with instant queries and sends `-datasource.queryStep` as the step, 5m by default, or `step` from the group `params`. VictoriaMetrics only uses the last sample before the window if it's at most one step before the window, so with a scrape interval longer than the step the window must be at least two scrape intervals minus the step. Set the window explicitly to make the rule independent of the step.
    diagnostics:
        - message: '`rate()` has no lookbehind window, so VictoriaMetrics uses a 5m window, the query step, default vmalert -datasource.queryStep (5m). `rate()` needs a window of at least 15m with samples of `foo` every 10m on `prom` VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com (its slowest series in the last 15m, measured with `scrape_interval()`; `scrapeInterval` in pint config is 1m), so it can return no results or wrong ones.'
          firstcolumn: 1
          lastcolumn: 9
          kind: 0
    lines:
        first: 2
        last: 2
    severity: 1
    anchor: 0

