[TestRateVMMeasuredInterval/window_shorter_than_the_measured_interval_allows - 1]
- description: window shorter than the measured interval allows
  content: |
    - record: foo:rate
      expr: rate(foo[2m])
  output: |
    2 |   expr: rate(foo[2m])
                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
                `rate()` needs a window of at least 15m with samples of `foo` every 10m on `prom`
                VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com (its slowest series in the last 15m,
                measured with `scrape_interval()`; `scrapeInterval` in pint config is 1m): vmalert evaluates
                the rule with instant queries with a 5m step, the query step, default vmalert
                -datasource.queryStep (5m), and VictoriaMetrics uses the last sample before the window only
                if it's at most 5m before the window. A `[2m]` window can have a single sample, so it can
                return no results or wrong ones.
